            <ArticleTitle>A novel approach for crossing a virtually occluded vessel using ultra-low-profile balloon backup.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>425-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We discuss a case in which a novel ultra-low-profile angioplasty balloon was used to provide wire backup by advancing the uninflated balloon nose into the entry point of a virtually occluded lesion. This enabled crossing of the lesion, and demonstrates how an improved balloon design can directly lead to improved clinical outcomes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
